{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt","id":688405,"title":"Quick Question: What do Werewolves hunt?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-04T09:27:44-07:00","id":688405,"title":"Quick Question: What do Werewolves hunt?","content":"Basically, do werewolves hunt 'bad' things or irregular things? Are they ensuring cosmic balance or nibbling on evil? If it is a per pack interpretation, what do the tribes teach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T09:56:37-07:00","id":688451,"title":"","content":"They hunt whatever's got the Shadow out of balance. Excess spirits, destabilizing humans, problematic suprnaturals, even other werewolves sometimes.<br /> <br /> Each Tribe hunts a different favored prey:<ul><li>Blood Talons hunt other wolves, usually ones who are making a mess for Forsaken society (read: the Pure)</li> <li>Bone Shadows hunt ephemeral creatures, usually disruptive spirits</li> <li>Hunters in Darkness hunt whatever messes up their turf, especially the Hosts.</li> <li>Iron Masters hunt humans, and are the most at-home in urban areas</li> <li>Storm Lords like to hunt Claimed</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 10-04-2015, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T10:23:19-07:00","id":688499,"title":"","content":"Short answer - <b>EVERYTHING</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In 2ED werewolves can even hunt abstract concepts, like &quot;clean streets&quot; of their territory. They even can declare this as Siskur-Dah ( 'Sacred Hunt' ) ritual target. But, most commonly, they hunt spirits, humans and various flesh-spirits hybrids ( like Hosts or Claimed ). It's logical, as Uratha are human-spirits hybrids themselves, so the are most dedicated to humans or spirits side of their nature.<br /> <br /> But in theory - <i>anything</i> can be target of Siskur-Dah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt#post688405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, do werewolves hunt 'bad' things or irregular things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both, depends how you can see them. To the Uratha 'bad' are irregular, as they break normal ecosystem they look for. Uratha can leave, for example, Vice spirits alone in bad part of town. At least till Gluttony, Greed or Lust spirits do not make all residents go to killng rage and by this move the local ecosystem to the unhealthy balance, with new murders and destruction spirits changing the local ecosystem. But as all spirits ( or <i><b>humans</b></i> ) are in the end egocentric, Uratha have paws full of work. ( And Chronicles to resolve by this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt#post688405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they ensuring cosmic balance or nibbling on evil?</div> </div> </div> </div>More they strive to &quot;cosmic balance&quot; - as hybrid race, Uratha likes things in the middle. See that in 2ED most optimal Harmony is in the center of the scale, at Harmony 5. Enoguth for Flesh and Spirit.<br /> <br /> Still, Malejins - Lords of Vices - are making broad moves to crush anything beside their favorit Sins - so they need to be stop, so some Virtues can blossom. But, in the end, werewolves target &quot;harmony&quot; - of predatory Bodhisattva human-wolf spirits hybrids. But Harmony, none the less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt#post688405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is a per pack interpretation, what do the tribes teach?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's even per wolf interpretation, but most packs are agreeing on general &quot;spectrum&quot; of what their will Hunt. City packs can hunt mainly humans and spirits, to even the ecosystem. But still one member that is Hunter in Darkness will look over Hosts, they will not invade their territory.<br /> <br /> In 2ED each Tribe has Sacred Prey - the target of their Hunt most worth of their time and dedication. Tribes teach techniques to hunt those beings, so large portion of Uratha join particular Tribe not even from philosophical matters - but practical. If young Rahu lost his beloved wife to the Rat Host, he will surely can join Hunters in Darkness, even if he does not look as the environmentalist or stealthy kind of guy - he just want to know how to fight Rats effectively to take revange, and it's all that is matter to choose this Tribe.<br /> <br /> <b>Sacred Preys for the Tribes of Moon</b><br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talons</b> - <i>Werewolves</i> - mainly Pure, Bale Hounds or those poor wolf souls that have lost their Harmony on the extremes ( Harmony 10 or 0 werewolves ). But sometimes even other wolves from the Tribes of the Moon.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Shadows</b> - <i>Spirits </i>- Shadow Realm should be understand and no one knows it better than Bone Shadows, to not make too much fall out from your actions.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter in Darkness</b> - <i>Hosts</i> - as most disrespecting local territory and almost always making bad things to sacred Gauntlet between Flesh and Spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Masters</b> - <i>Humans</i> - Thinking Ape is most cunning being and enormously outnumber any other being on Earth. Humans, if they would know, could easily crash any Uratha society. You must be cleverest hunter to hunt inside them and not be caught.<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Lords</b> - <i>Urged and Claimed</i> - unholy merging of both things that should not be whole. Especially, as they look to much like werewolves themselves... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472272#post472272\"><b>our older topic </b>we talk extensively on various subjects of Siskur-Dah</a> and possible targets ( also with devs ) - I advice to read it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-04-2015, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T10:37:26-07:00","id":688510,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the replies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, in short, there is no evil spirits or even people <i>per sey; </i>just something unpleasant that needs correcting. In a sense, all wolves are stewards combating pollution, where pollution is an undesired change to the environment and the wolves themselves decide what is desired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T10:42:19-07:00","id":688512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt?p=688451#post688451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They hunt whatever's got the Shadow out of balance. Excess spirits, destabilizing humans, problematic suprnaturals, even other werewolves sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind though, different packs will have different definitions of &quot;balance&quot;, depending on the spiritual resonance they want to cultivate in their territory. Even a single pack with a large territory might want to maintain different resonances in different parts of their territory.<br /> <br /> The short answer is, werewolves hunt anything they don't want in their territory. For some packs that might mean hunting murder spirits and cereal killers and homocidal predator kings. For others, it might mean hunting order spirits and police and hierarchal ivory claws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T11:06:47-07:00","id":688520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt?p=688510#post688510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the replies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, in short, there is no evil spirits or even people <i>per sey; </i>just something unpleasant that needs correcting. In a sense, all wolves are stewards combating pollution, where pollution is an undesired change to the environment and the wolves themselves decide what is desired.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T11:14:30-07:00","id":688544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt?p=688510#post688510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in short, there is no evil spirits or even people <i>per sey; </i>just something unpleasant that needs correcting. In a sense, all wolves are stewards combating pollution, where pollution is an undesired change to the environment and the wolves themselves decide what is desired.</div> </div> </div> </div>There <b>are</b> evil spirits, per sey, they are called <i>Malejins</i> and their lower lot, <i>Malinets</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They tend to make Loci in to Wounds and pollute the <i>Hisil</i>.<br /> <br /> But no - they are not automatic enemies of the werewolves. Tribes of Moon and even Pure fight them as most are to obsessed with their Sins, and by this cross Uratha way of ruling territory. But it's not more major threat than dedicated to a cause human, Mysteries driven wizard or even just very problematic spirit. In the end, every enemy of the pack is chosen individually.<br /> <br /> And what are targets for Siskur-Dah is chosen with contrast of how Uratha want to rule territory, as pointed by <b>Charlaquin</b>. Each pack choose the vision of their &quot;perfect territory&quot;, and takes one by one threats to it. Want Order to rule - destroy spirits of anarchy, make humans organisation more prominent, take care of those pesky things coming on &quot;our way&quot;. Want Happiness to rule territory? Destroy spirits of sadness, make some activities humans will be joyful around, even <i>invite </i>the Host connected with bliss.<br /> <br /> It's even why Protectorates are called for in <b>Werewolf</b> 2ED. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &quot;Hosts are massively attacking the city? Call the Packs, we need to resolve this, in coordination.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-04-2015, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T12:11:18-07:00","id":688573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt?p=688544#post688544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <b>are</b> evil spirits, per sey, they are called <i>Malejins</i> and their lower lot, <i>Malinets</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They tend to make Loci in to Wounds and pollute the <i>Hisil</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although, wether or not they are technically spirits is up for debate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T12:22:21-07:00","id":688585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt?p=688573#post688573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, wether or not they are technically spirits is up for debate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If it looks like a duck spirit, quacks like a duck spirit, it's probably a duck spirit.<br /> <br /> It might not be, but it probably is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T13:26:05-07:00","id":688680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt?p=688544#post688544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There <b>are</b> evil spirits, per sey, they are called <i>Malejins</i> and their lower lot, <i>Malinets</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They tend to make Loci in to Wounds and pollute the <i>Hisil</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are the guys who caused my confusion as it happens. They suggested that there was a good-over-bad by calling destructive spirits negative. Is there the inverse to Malejin in the Hisil or are Malejin bad because they aren't (wholly) spirits? (hehe, bad because not holy. :P )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T13:36:58-07:00","id":688684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt?p=688585#post688585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it looks like a duck spirit, quacks like a duck spirit, it's probably a duck spirit.<br /> <br /> It might not be, but it probably is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Part of the issue with the Maeljin and wounded spirits is that they do not 'quack like a duck.' They don't act like regular spirits. Even the Banish rite, which pushes spirits out of the real world and into the Hisil, is specifically called out to not push them into the Hisil, but somewhere else.<br /> <br /> As explained by a writer, Chris Allen, <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;So, Wounded spirits aren't 'bad' spirits. They're </span></span></span><i>corrupted</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. Hatred, anger, death, murder, pain, anguish spirits are all perfectly normal spirits. The creatures that infest the pustules of taint that are Wounds have been infected and changed. A Wounded spirit of happiness would be hurled through a Wound by the Banish rite; an unWounded spirit of hatred would not.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whether a werewolf decides to hunt them is up to the werewolf. Destruction is part of nature just as creation is, and both can be bad when driven to extremes. Even if things are drastically unbalanced, a werewolf does not <i>have </i>to hunt them. In fact a werewolf might let something like that occur just so they can have a more powerful spirit to hunt in the future.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-04-2015, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T13:58:01-07:00","id":688720,"title":"","content":"Thank you. What was once cloudy is now clear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T14:24:44-07:00","id":688765,"title":"","content":"The other thing I <i>believe</i> is on the Hunt This, It's Corrupt list: Magath. They're not mentioned much in the 2e core, so I just know what I've picked up here and there - people may be about to correct me on some of this. ;-)<br /> <br /> A Magath is a spirit that's become a strange hybrid by feeding on essence that doesn't suit it. This is quite a conceptual thing - a dog spirit can feed on loyalty spirits and become a loyal dog spirit, or on wrath spirits and become a furious dog spirit. That's fine, both are aspects of Dog, so this isn't a problem. But when a spirit is starved of essence that suits it, it might feed on something that it can't digest properly - like a Happiness spirit stuck in a mouldering wasteland where there aren't any people, where all it can get is Decay essence.<br /> <br /> When this happens, the spirit changes into a weird hybrid spirit. I'm not sure how this manifests (and would welcome someone explaining, I'm curious :-) ) but I'm fairly sure it's something most werewolves see as a breach of the natural order and worth hunting down to destroy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T15:04:01-07:00","id":688837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt?p=688765#post688765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing I <i>believe</i> is on the Hunt This, It's Corrupt list: Magath. They're not mentioned much in the 2e core, so I just know what I've picked up here and there - people may be about to correct me on some of this. ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>They were presented this way earlier on in 1e. Nowadays it's less that they're inherently corrupt and more that a spirit with multiple influences that are completely unrelated is likely to do weird things to the local shadowscape to get the resonances it needs. Most packs aren't going to want something like that mucking up their territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt?p=688765#post688765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Magath is a spirit that's become a strange hybrid by feeding on essence that doesn't suit it. This is quite a conceptual thing - a dog spirit can feed on loyalty spirits and become a loyal dog spirit, or on wrath spirits and become a furious dog spirit. That's fine, both are aspects of Dog, so this isn't a problem. But when a spirit is starved of essence that suits it, it might feed on something that it can't digest properly - like a Happiness spirit stuck in a mouldering wasteland where there aren't any people, where all it can get is Decay essence.<br /> <br /> When this happens, the spirit changes into a weird hybrid spirit. I'm not sure how this manifests (and would welcome someone explaining, I'm curious :-) )</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally, spirits will only feed on essence that resonates with their influences. If for some reason a spirit is forced to feed on essence with resonance that clashes with their influences, its nature has to shift to accommodate that new type of resonance. This would be reflected by gaining a new Influence. Basically, magath are built just like normal spirits, but they have Influences that don't relate to each other, like your example of Happiness and Decay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/688405-quick-question-what-do-werewolves-hunt?p=688765#post688765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but I'm fairly sure it's something most werewolves see as a breach of the natural order and worth hunting down to destroy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are a bit of a breach of the natural order, in the sense that they don't often occur naturally. But they're more just weird than bad. Werewolves might want to want to hunt one because it's making it hard to cultivate consistent types of resonance, but they probably wouldn't feel the need to put them down on principle. Maybe in a &quot;we should put this wretched creature out of its misery&quot; kind of way, but not because they're necessarily bad or evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T17:57:52-07:00","id":689045,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Basically a werewolf <i>can </i>hunt and kill everything they view as wrong or impure, but not all werewolves are going to agree on what's wrong and impure, or whether that means they should be hunted. A werewolf who performs the sacred hunt only to kill magath because they're 'wrong' has their own view of what the hunt is about, and it is likely the sort of thing that would reflect itself in their life outside of the hunt.<br /> <br /> It's all very fun, and the hunt and how they view it allows for a lot of depth for werewolf characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T16:09:55-07:00","id":690549,"title":"","content":"Thanks for explaining! And that gives me some ideas I should let percolate through for a while. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}